  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "This is the right fix for the  `AttnResPipelineStage.forward_one_chunk` in #4312:\r\n\r\nFollowed comment in: https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/4312#discussion_r3987651867 to avoid intrusive changes in `pipeline_parallel.py`,\r\n\r\nit added the same line, under the same condition, that the base `PipelineStage.forward_one_chunk` gained when pytorch/pytorch#196640 relanded on Sept 29, and the matching reset stays in the base `wait_for_gradient_reduction` / `clear_runtime_states`, which `AttnResPipelineStage` does not override.\r\n\r\nThe B200 `kimi_k3_fsdp2_tp2_ep2_pp2_vpp4` cell stayed green because the B200 lane installs cu130 nightlies, which jump from `dev20260928` to `dev20261003`, so every run until today (including the `ciflow/b200` run on #4731) had no manual finalization. With `dev20261003`, the cell's recipe on main fails at the first `REDUCE_GRAD` with \"FSDP finalize_backward requires manual backward finalization\".\r\n\r\nThe root cause is in #4312: `AttnResPipelineStage.forward_one_chunk` copies the base forward, so it misses whatever the base adds (this line, `register_forward_context`), and it writes the base's private `_forward_chunk_states`, which #4661 had to do the update also. \r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThanks a lot for fixing Shuhua @shuhuayu and please LMK your thoughts on the following plan:\r\n\r\nAfter this lands I will send a follow-up that overrides `_retrieve_recv_activations` (assemble the block stack) and `forward_maybe_with_nosync` (commit the stage's blocks and pack the payload) instead, so the stage runs the base forward and the line added here can go.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-04T07:14:34Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5025#issuecomment-5977615449",
      "id": 5977615449,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-04T07:14:34Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "QIU023"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @QIU023, thanks for the followup and sorry for the late reply. this has been fixed in another replicate pr: https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5142, so i will close this.",
